d here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 168% of normal in May to June but just 35% in November to December. Grid 12735 had its driest year in 1988 at 50%. On grid 13036 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 36.8, and that is a NOAA figure, not RMA&rsquo;s index.</p>"}
